//@version=5
// =====================================================================================================
//#{W
//  ICT SWING model (US100)  -  Python: swing_snap.py
//  Generated from pine/core.pine by pine/build.py - edit core.pine, then rebuild the scripts.
//  US100 ONLY (default). 5m chart recommended (1m-1H work). HTF data from request.security() on COMPLETED candles (no repaint).
//  Rule 1  Liquidity: D / W / M swings (2 each side), 4H swings (10 each side), fresh 4H FVG far edges.
//  Rule 2  A 1H candle wicks through a Rule 1 level and closes back.
//  Rule 3  The last 4H FVG of the sweeping leg (formed into the sweep, within 10 4H candles, intact) is inverted by a 1H CLOSE
//          with 1H displacement and a 1H MSS.
//  Rule 4  Two entries per setup: a limit at the 4H IFVG near edge, and a limit at a 1H breaker FVG. Both valid 48 h.
//  Rule 5  Stop: 50% of the 1H order block of the drop (none: previous 1H candle high/low), no buffer.
//  Rule 6  Target: the 1H swing low before the 4H FVG's middle candle (Fixed R optional). Breakeven at +1R, then trail to each new 1H swing.
//#}
//#{N
//  ICT INTRADAY model (US100, 5m chart)  -  Python: intraday_snap.py
//  Generated from pine/core.pine by pine/build.py - edit core.pine, then rebuild the scripts.
//  US100 ONLY (default). HTF data from request.security() on COMPLETED candles (no repaint). SHORT described, LONG mirrored.
//  Rule 1  Liquidity: D / W / M swings (2 each side), 4H and 1H swings (10 each side), fresh 4H and 1H FVG far edges, previous
//          Asia / London / NY session highs/lows (New York clock) that are also a 1H+ swing, valid 7 days.
//  Rule 2  Sweep (5m): (A) a 5m candle wicks above a Rule 1 swing and closes back below, or (B) 1-2 5m candles close above it and are
//          followed by two strong bearish displacement candles, the second closing below the low of the first sweeping candle.
//  Rule 3  5m IFVG = the intact bullish 5m FVG nearest below the sweep (last 48 5m candles). BOS level = the lowest low between the
//          previous 5m swing high and the sweep extreme. 5m breaker = the last bearish 5m candle at or before that low.
//  Rule 4  Reversal within N 5m candles: closes below the 5m IFVG and below the BOS level, with displacement (2 candles >= 1 ATR,
//          or 1 candle with a body >= 1 ATR).
//  Rule 5  Entry: sell limit at the bottom of the latest bearish 5m FVG or 5m volume imbalance in the drop from the sweep extreme,
//          valid 60 minutes; cancelled if a candle opens above the stop.
//  Rule 6  Stop: the 5m breaker high (no buffer).
//  Rule 7  Target: fixed R (3R) or the major 5m swing (10 each side; none -> 3R). Breakeven at +1R.
//  Bias    The last sweep of a Rule 1 swing (D/W/M/4H/1H): high swept = bearish, low swept = bullish. Trades only with the bias.
//#}
// =====================================================================================================
//#I indicator("ICT Sweep > IFVG > MSS (rules 1-7)", shorttitle="ICT IFVG", overlay=true, max_boxes_count=500, max_lines_count=500, max_labels_count=500, max_bars_back=3000)
//#S strategy("ICT Sweep > IFVG > MSS Strategy (rules 1-7)", shorttitle="ICT IFVG Strategy", overlay=true, pyramiding=5, initial_capital=10000, default_qty_type=strategy.fixed, commission_type=strategy.commission.cash_per_contract, commission_value=0, slippage=0, max_boxes_count=500, max_lines_count=500, max_labels_count=500, max_bars_back=3000)

